    "terrainName": "berlin",
    "description": "What: Simulated devices SD-S1 (§5a). A scripted trainee possesses the Observer, who holds a laser rangefinder, binds his view to it, and AIMS his look at three named markers - men standing 200 m east, 450 m north-east and 900 m east of him - pressing RANGE at each: the device points where he looks (DevicePose from the station's look), the muscle traces its laser (LaserSpotSystem) and the device reads the spot that answers its request. Judge: (1) after each RANGE the device's LastRange is that marker's distance (within 3 m - the laser meets the near side of a man's body, the origin is the device); (2) the laser met THAT marker (the device's LastHit, copied from LaserSpot.Points[0].Hit); (3) the HUD bound to the device shows the range. Fail: no range, the wrong distance, the wrong man, or terrain. Check: scripts/scenario-regression.sh dv-range-targets"
  },
